2. Must Must follow below rules when generating text data:
Different groups of data are distinguished by line breaks.
Different contents of the same group of data are distinguished by |.
Make sure: The "|" character is used only to separate distinct contents within a same group.
EXAMPLE:
a|b|c
1|2|3
If a part of the data within a group also needs to be separated, use a symbol other than "|", to avoid confusion.
EXAMPLE:
a|b|c1,c2,c3
a|b|c1,c2,c3
in this example, it use "," to seperate c1 and c2 and c3.
avoid use ":", it confuses with time expression.

