       self.assertIn('Username already exists', error_element.text)
       ```

Common Root Cause:
All three errors are related to timing/synchronization issues in the Selenium tests. The tests are trying to interact with elements that either:
1. Have become stale due to page updates
2. Haven't fully loaded yet
3. Need to be re-located after page changes

Recommendations:
1. Add more explicit waits for elements to be present/clickable
2. Re-locate elements after page changes rather than reusing old references
3. Consider adding unique IDs to key elements for more reliable locating
4. Add small delays between critical operations if needed

The application code itself appears functionally correct - these are primarily test synchronization issues rather than application bugs. The test coverage is good (9 functionality tests), with 6 passing successfully, indicating the core functionality works as expected.
