```python
ROUTE /dashboard (GET)
    IF user not logged in: REDIRECT /login
    READ saved_tips.txt FOR user's saved tips
    RENDER dashboard.html WITH username AND saved_tips

ROUTE /get_tips (POST)
    IF user not logged in: REDIRECT /login
    GET destination AND interests FROM form
    READ tips_database.txt
    FILTER tips WHERE destination matches AND interest in interests
    GENERATE tip IDs AS "destination_interest"
    RENDER tips.html WITH filtered tips
```
Key Libraries:
- Flask: Handles routing and session management
- File I/O: Plain text files used as simple database

```python
CLASS TravelTipper:
    METHOD get_tips(destination, interests):
        OPEN tips.txt
        FOR EACH line IN file:
            SPLIT line INTO tip_dest, category, content
            IF (destination MATCHES tip_dest) AND 
               (interests EMPTY OR ANY interest MATCHES category):
                ADD {'destination': tip_dest, 'category': category, 'content': content} TO tips
        RETURN tips

ROUTE /tips (POST):
    IF NOT logged_in: REDIRECT /login
    GET destination FROM form
    GET interests FROM form (split by comma)
    CALL get_tips(destination, interests)
    RENDER tips.html WITH tips
```

