## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:save_favorite_tips  
Failure/Error Analysis1: Dashboard link not found after saving a favorite.  
Improvement Guidance1: Add a success message or redirect after saving favorites to ensure state consistency. Atomic File Operations: Ensure `favorites.txt` writes are completed before rendering updates.  
Failure/Error Analysis2: Race condition between saving favorites and page updates. Favorites management lacks atomic operations. No feedback mechanism after save operation.  
Improvement Guidance2: Implement proper redirect-after-POST pattern. Add visual feedback for successful save operations. Consider using database transactions for file operations. Ensure UI state updates consistently after backend operations.  

2. |Case|:user_registration  
Failure/Error Analysis1: Duplicate username error message not displayed. File Handling: `register_user()` may not properly detect existing usernames due to file cursor issues. Error Propagation: Flask route does not guarantee error message rendering.  
Improvement Guidance1: Use `with open()` in `r+` mode to read/write atomically. Lock files during operations to prevent race conditions. Return structured error codes (e.g., "USER_EXISTS") from `register_user()`. Ensure templates always render errors when `error` parameter is passed.  
Failure/Error Analysis2: Test expects page title containing "Registration". Actual title is "Travel Tipper - Register" (register.html). Functional registration works (duplicate check passes).  
Improvement Guidance2: Establish naming convention for UI elements early. Maintain consistency between route names (/register), page titles, and test expectations. Consider centralized title management.  
Failure/Error Analysis3: Error handling flow needs improvement. Registration feedback mechanism incomplete. No proper validation before file operations.  
Improvement Guidance3: Implement comprehensive form validation. Improve error message rendering mechanism. Add proper locking for user file operations. Consider adding client-side validation before submission.  

